    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const alaRecord = $('Step 9a - Fetch ALA Record').first().json;\nconst rawText = alaRecord['Raw Tex'] || alaRecord['Raw Text'] || 'Not available';\n\nconst recentRecords = $('Step 9a-2 - Fetch Recent RDA Drafts').first().json;\nconst recentList = recentRecords.list || [];\nconst recentOpenings = [];\nfor (let i = 0; i < recentList.length; i++) {\n  const draft = recentList[i]['Public Response Draft'];\n  if (draft && draft.length > 10) {\n    const firstSentence = draft.split(/[.!—]/)[0].trim();\n    if (firstSentence.length > 5) recentOpenings.push(firstSentence);\n  }\n}\n\nconst inp = $('Step 8 - Build Final Output').first().json;\nif (!inp.public_response_draft || inp.public_response_draft.length < 20)\n  throw new Error('public_response_draft missing or too short from Step 8. ala_record_id: ' + inp.ala_record_id);\n\nconst audit_system_prompt =\n'Role: Audit the public response against the original guest review. Preserve human quality. If all checks pass, return unchanged. If any check fails, correct ONLY the failing element. Never rewrite passing content or invent details.\\n\\n' +\n'COMPLIANCE:\\n' +\n'1. NAMED STAFF: If the review names staff, the exact name must appear in the draft; never replace it with a generic reference.\\n' +\n'2. REVIEW DEPTH: Reviews over 80 words must reference at least 2 specific guest-named elements. Short reviews must not receive padded responses.\\n' +\n'3. CLOSING: Closing must derive from the review: occasion, dish, guest wording, or visit frequency. Fail generic closings, repeated nouns from earlier in the draft, or vague closings like \"all of it\", \"across both\", \"that same experience\", or \"that kind of evening\". For very short reviews, close with a brief sincere acknowledgment, not a formula.\\n' +\n'4. LOYALTY: If the guest signals repeat/frequent visits (always, every time, weekly, regularly, each visit, been here before), acknowledge the ongoing relationship.\\n' +\n'5. SUGGESTION: If the guest makes a specific positive suggestion, acknowledge it by name.\\n' +\n'6. PROHIBITED: Remove email addresses, URLs, contact methods/channels, placeholders, and \"We apologize for any inconvenience\".\\n\\n' +\n'FORMULA:\\n' +\n'7. OVERUSED VERBS: Fail if \"landed\" appears more than once or is the primary acknowledgment verb. Replace with natural alternatives such as resonated, came through, delivered, felt right, worked, made an impression, held up, or came together.\\n' +\n'8. OVERUSED PHRASES: Replace formulaic phrases with specific language: \"means a great deal to our team\", \"our team works hard to\", \"all of it\", \"that kind of evening\", \"exactly what we work toward\". Never open with \"Knowing\".\\n' +\n'9. BRAND PHRASES: At most one may appear: \"Thank you for dining with us\", \"We\\\\\\'d love to welcome you back\", \"We take great pride in every guest experience\". Keep only the most natural one or remove all.\\n\\n' +\n'OPENING:\\n' +\n'10. REPETITION: If recent openings are provided, fail if this opening repeats their lead word or grammatical structure. Rewrite the opening only.\\n\\n' +\n'GUEST NAME:\\n' +\n'11. If GUEST NAME is not \"Not available\", it must appear in the draft. If missing, insert only in the opening. T1: \"[Name],\" at the start. T2/T3: \"Hello [Name] ---\" before the existing opening.\\n\\n' +\n'Correction Rules: Correct only failed elements. Preserve tone_style, formality_level, and brand voice. The final draft must pass all checklist items.\\n';\n\nconst recentOpeningsBlock = recentOpenings.length > 0\n  ? '\\n\\nRECENT OPENINGS USED — do not repeat these structures:\\n' +\n    recentOpenings.map((o, i) => (i + 1) + '. \"' + o + '\"').join('\\n')\n  : '';\n\nconst closingBlock =\n'\\n\\nJSON RULES:\\n' +\n'- Return valid JSON only. No preamble, explanation, or markdown fences.\\n' +\n'- failed_items must contain checklist item NAMES as strings, never numbers.\\n' +\n'- Use straight double quotes only.\\n' +\n'- Do not truncate final_public_response_draft.\\n\\n' +\n'RETURN exactly:\\n' +\n'{\\n' +\n'  \"audit_passed\": true,\\n' +\n'  \"failed_items\": [],\\n' +\n'  \"final_public_response_draft\": \"complete corrected or unchanged public draft here\"\\n' +\n'}';\n\nconst audit_system_prompt_final = audit_system_prompt + recentOpeningsBlock + closingBlock;\n\nconst audit_user_prompt =\n'ORIGINAL GUEST REVIEW:\\n' + rawText + '\\n\\n' +\n'PROPOSED PUBLIC RESPONSE DRAFT:\\n' + inp.public_response_draft + '\\n\\n' +\n'GUEST NAME: ' + ((inp.reviewer_handle && !inp.reviewer_handle.toLowerCase().includes('review') && !inp.reviewer_handle.toLowerCase().startsWith('anonymous')) ? inp.reviewer_handle : 'Not available') + '\\n' +\n'RESPONSE TIER: ' + inp.confirmed_response_tier + '\\n' +\n'TONE STYLE: ' + inp.tone_style + '\\n\\n' +\n'Run the audit checklist. Return JSON only.';\n\nconst audit_request_body = JSON.stringify({\n  model: 'claude-sonnet-4-6',\n  max_tokens: 1500,\n  temperature: 0,\n  system: audit_system_prompt_final,\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: audit_user_prompt }]\n});\n\nreturn [{ json: {\n  bra_record_id: inp.bra_record_id,\n  confirmed_response_tier: inp.confirmed_response_tier,\n  governance_flag: inp.governance_flag,\n  human_review_required: inp.human_review_required,\n  solution_type: inp.solution_type,\n  emotional_axis: inp.emotional_axis,\n  pain_axis: inp.pain_axis,\n  stability_axis: inp.stability_axis,\n  signal_based_consideration: inp.signal_based_consideration,\n  tone_style: inp.tone_style,\n  urgency_level: inp.urgency_level,\n  commercial_risk_flag: inp.commercial_risk_flag,\n  behavioral_interpretation: inp.behavioral_interpretation,\n  lang: inp.lang,\n  client_id: inp.client_id,\n  enriched_emotion_tag: inp.enriched_emotion_tag,\n  enriched_pain_point: inp.enriched_pain_point,\n  pain_point_sub_category: inp.pain_point_sub_category,\n  signal_type: inp.signal_type,\n  intensity_level: inp.intensity_level,\n  hsi_record_id: inp.hsi_record_id,\n  ess_record_id: inp.ess_record_id,\n  eip_record_id: inp.eip_record_id,\n  ala_record_id: inp.ala_record_id,\n  prior_run_id: inp.prior_run_id,\n  reviewer_handle: inp.reviewer_handle,\n  emotion_hypothesis: inp.emotion_hypothesis,\n  keywords: inp.keywords,\n  brand_voice: inp.brand_voice,\n  brand_voice_brief: inp.brand_voice_brief,\n  lang_resolved: inp.lang_resolved,\n  generation_draft: inp.public_response_draft,\n  seo_keywords_used: inp.seo_keywords_used,\n  audit_request_body: audit_request_body\n} }];"
